 we can  predict our emission how long a patient  was going to stay  in hospital  so before we get too much into the  detail of that i'm going to share a  definition  of what we actually mean by a fake data  generator  so a fake data generator is a data set  generated at random with the purpose of  testing code the data set will contain  the same number of fields and same data  types as the original data but will not  replicate any relationships or patterns  found in the original data set so for  example the data that was originally  used to train a data data science model  um  isn't isn't isn't isn't using this and  the fake data is generated independently  of the original data set  um  one of the reasons why we can't  anonymize the set is because of  well the data that we deal with is very  sensitive  um  we're dealing with health data so we  can't really publish that even if we  anonymized it would have to go through a  lot of approval  and rightly so in terms of information  governance making sure that we've  covered across everything by gdpr by  having fake data generators it allows us  to be a lot more open in terms of what  we can share  fab so why do we need a fake data  generator which kind of answers your  question so thank you for leading me on  nicely to the next slide  um  so  when  gloucestershire applied augusta  hospitals applied  last year about their idea about whether  we can predict patients who can long  stay  and that's when when you say long stay  we mean patients who stay over 21 days  in hospital  it was a really important problem that  we knew  that would affect other trust and that  if we  um this project could really benefit  other trusts across the nhs  um prolonged stays in hospital can be um  bad for patients especially those who  are frail and elderly and there's one  journal that reported that 10 10 extra  days in hostel can be a deterioration of  about 10 years especially in patients  who are elderly  so what we wanted to do was hav