at might be considered as an  improvement on  me on fake data  so why would you use synthetic data so  the main problem as we've sort of  touched on in this presentation so far  is that fake data limits capabilities  what you can do with a code release  it stops you from assessing model  performance and understanding exactly  how well the model works  so the big benefit of using something  like synthetic data is that it enables  users to understand how well your model  works and maybe see a more  realistic output from your model rather  than just something that is a jumbled  set from the from the fake data you've  put in however there's substantial  challenges associated with fake data as  well so information governance is a big  thing working in healthcare and using  synthetic data only mitigates some of  the information governance challenges um  there's still information governance  associated with synthetic data  so if that's a problem with your real  data uh synthetic data might not solve  it  bottom two are kind of interlinked so  generating and evaluating synthetic that  can be quite tricky and there isn't  really any standards for evaluating  synthetic data so it can be quite  difficult to know if what you've  produced is good or works or is  appropriate  we in the schoolworks team were  interested in exploring synthetic data  and an opportunity came up working with  the analytics unit at the nhs um and  they were looking to undertake a  specific project which needed a nice  varied rich set of synthetic data  and also the scope works team supported  them by developing a pipeline which  we're going to explain in the rest of  this presentation to produce data that  met their needs um we used a synthetic  data generation model called synth vae  which you can see details on the right  hand side  that was generated by the analytics unit  um and we took our model and fitted it  into a reusable pipeline um that went  end-to-end to generate and evaluate  synthetic da