ces output data that looks like  your training data originally  so i'll hand back to jennifer to talk  about  the evaluation stage of the project  [Applause]  thank you matt so i'm going to talk  about how we evaluate synthetic data how  do we make sure  that what the output is looks it looks  good  um and we classify sort of evaluations  to three different concepts so we have  utility  quality and  privacy so utility  is about what the data is actually going  to be used for so we need to think about  what the purpose is is it going to be  data that we're going to give to someone  who wants to try and get insights in  terms of correlations between different  variables or is it someone who just  wants to test whether data can flow  through an app so there's different  levels in which  the quality is needed which actually  feeds into the next one which is about  quality and is the date is the synthetic  data a good enough representation  of the original data to do the work that  we want to do  so how much ground truth is still in  that synthetic data  and i'm going to talk a little bit more  about some of the tests in a second  about how we actually look and measure  some of the quality and the last one is  privacy which is again incredibly  important especially in healthcare so  how do we make sure the synthetic data  isn't giving anything away with the  original data how do we make sure that  now there's no leakage in terms from the  original data set and it's particularly  important so who's going to have access  to that data set and i think to the  first question  you know if it's going to be up to  everyone are you going to have to go  through some kind of approval process to  be able to access that data there's all  these things that we need to think about  before actually generating the data  and here are some metrics that we  actually included in our synthetic data  repo  this isn't all of them but this is some  of the high level ones so we have things  like c